## Process Due Recurring Use Case — process_due_recurring.dart
```dart
// Called on every app launch in main.dart or app.dart
// Checks all active recurring transactions and auto-adds overdue ones

class ProcessDueRecurring {
  final RecurringRepository recurringRepo;
  final TransactionRepository transactionRepo;

  ProcessDueRecurring(this.recurringRepo, this.transactionRepo);

  Future<void> call() async {
    final now = DateTime.now();
    final due = await recurringRepo.getDueRecurring(now);

    for (final r in due) {
      // Create actual transaction from recurring template
      final tx = Transaction(
        id: const Uuid().v4(),
        type: r.type,
        amount: r.amount,
        categoryId: r.categoryId,
        walletId: r.walletId,
        date: now,
        notes: r.notes ?? r.label,
        createdAt: now,
      );
      await transactionRepo.addTransaction(tx);
      await recurringRepo.markAsProcessed(r.id, now);
    }
  }
}
```

## Call on App Launch — app.dart
```dart
// In app.dart initState or router redirect
ref.read(processDueRecurringProvider).call();
```

## Screen Specifications

### recurring_page.dart
- Accessed from Settings screen → "Recurring Transactions"
- AppBar: large title "Recurring"
- List of recurring items using RecurringItem widget
- Each item: label, frequency badge, amount, next due date, active toggle
- FAB: "+" → add_recurring_page.dart
- Swipe to delete with confirmation dialog
- Empty state: "No recurring transactions set up"

### add_recurring_page.dart
- Modal bottom sheet (isScrollControlled: true)
- Label: TextField (e.g. "Netflix", "Gaji")
- Type: SegmentedButton Expense | Income
- Amount: numeric input (formatRupiah)
- Category picker: same grid as Add Transaction
- Wallet picker: same as Add Transaction
- Frequency: SegmentedButton Daily | Weekly | Monthly | Yearly
- Day of month: number picker (shown only for Monthly/Yearly)
- Start date: DatePicker
- End date: DatePicker (optional, toggle to enable)
- Save button: full-width black ElevatedButton

